<title>FRANCE: Generale shares jump on health deal.</title>
<headline>Generale shares jump on health deal.</headline>
<dateline>PARIS 1997-07-02</dateline>
<text>
<p>Shares in Generale des Eaux gained some 2.65 percent on Wednesday, in a higher market, on the conclusion of the sale of its health activities to Cinven, dealers said.</p>
<p>At 0956, Generale was up 2.65 percent at 775 francs ($132).</p>
<p>Cinven called the deal, for 1.1 billion pounds ($1.8 billion), the largest European management buy-out of the decade because it is financing the deal for the management of Generale units Generale de Sante and General Healthcare Group.</p>
<p>Generale des Eaux said it expected a debt reduction of nearly seven billion francs from the sale.</p>
<p>($ = 5.884 French Francs)</p>
<p>($ = 0.602 British Pounds)</p>
